 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "be going to로 계획 말하기",
   "en": "'be going to' for plans"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "이미 정한 계획이나 곧 일어날 일은 be going to + 동사 원형으로 말합니다. be동사는 주어에 맞게 am / is / are로 바꿉니다. 부정은 be 뒤에 not, 의문문은 be를 앞으로 보냅니다.",
   "en": "Use 'be going to' + base verb for plans you have already made and for things that are about to happen. 'Be' changes with the subject: am / is / are. For a negative add 'not' after 'be'; for a question put 'be' first."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "주어 / Subject",
    "긍정 / Positive",
    "부정 / Negative",
    "의문 / Question"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "I",
     "I'm going to work",
     "I'm not going to work",
     "Am I going to work?"
    ],
    [
     "you / we / they",
     "We're going to work",
     "We aren't going to work",
     "Are you going to work?"
    ],
    [
     "he / she / it",
     "She's going to work",
     "She isn't going to work",
     "Is she going to work?"
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "미래를 나타내는 말: tomorrow, tonight, next week, soon.",
    "en": "Future time words: tomorrow, tonight, next week, soon."
   },
   {
    "ko": "going to 뒤에는 동사 원형: I'm going to buy (✕ buying).",
    "en": "After going to use the base verb: I'm going to buy (not buying)."
   },
   {
    "ko": "'go'와 함께 쓰면 going to go도 가능합니다: We're going to go home.",
    "en": "With 'go' you can say going to go: We're going to go home."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
   {
    "t": "I am going to work tomorrow.",
    "ko": "저는 내일 일할 거예요."
   },
   {
    "t": "She is going to visit Paris next week.",
    "ko": "그녀는 다음 주에 파리에 갈 거예요."
   },
   {
    "t": "We are going to watch a film tonight.",
    "ko": "우리는 오늘 밤 영화를 볼 거예요."
   },
   {
    "t": "They aren't going to travel.",
    "ko": "그들은 여행하지 않을 거예요."
   },
   {
    "t": "What are you going to do tomorrow?",
    "ko": "내일 뭐 할 거예요?"
   }
  ],
